{"term":"appeal","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4a035fe365bf8e325e","definition":"An application to a superior court or judge for a decision or order by an inferior court or judge to be reviewed and overturned.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["appeal court","appeals court","appeal to authority","appeal to emotion","appeal to motive","appeal to nature","counterappeal","court of appeal","curb appeal","sex appeal","street appeal","whip appeal","cross-appeal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appeal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7168e81fbdf114a879","definition":"The legal document or form by which such an application is made; also, the court case in which the application is argued.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["appeal court","appeals court","appeal to authority","appeal to emotion","appeal to motive","appeal to nature","counterappeal","court of appeal","curb appeal","sex appeal","street appeal","whip appeal","cross-appeal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appeal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be8f45b0b4979ad19c","definition":"A person's legal right to apply to court for such a review.","example":"I have an appeal against the lower court decision.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["appeal court","appeals court","appeal to authority","appeal to emotion","appeal to motive","appeal to nature","counterappeal","court of appeal","curb appeal","sex appeal","street appeal","whip appeal","cross-appeal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribut